.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:675:- FIX: bidirectional inventory — `ScannedFiles` floor ("scanned no production sources; the check is blind"), empty-sites floor ("derived no refusal sites; the scan is blind"), and a reverse check requiring every exercised site to resolve to a derived site. The reverse bound is derived from the test run, not hand-listed, so truncation reddens without a magic number. Floors that must survive early-return mutants live at the caller (`TestSection71AdvertisesNoPublicSDK` for `exportedSymbols`); a floor inside the helper is bypassed by `return nil` at its top. `auditRefusalInventory` floors live in the audit itself, so they hold for the same reason.
.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:676:- FINDING: the production `OSSystem` seam had zero negative tests — eight survivors in one file. Three are entry 0230's uid-0 twin on the attestation side (`Inspect` swallowing the error as uid 0, `fileOwnerUID` returning `0, nil` against its own doc comment, `CurrentOperatorPolicy` seeding `{0}`), one inverts the headline invariant at the only violable point (`ReadDir` error as absence). The `Inspect` attestation-error branch is unreachable with real stat results on unix, so it is forced through a documented `ownerAttester` variable — the only seam that makes the branch testable rather than merely readable.
.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:678:- EVIDENCE: 19-mutant harness over every rev4 survivor shape: 18 RED, 1 environment-equivalent green (G40b). `go test ./...` exit 0, provider cover 97.0%, `go vet`/`GOOS=windows go vet`/`GOOS=windows go build` clean.
.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:688:- EVIDENCE: reviewer batteries re-run — battery-1 46 killed/0 survived (12 formulation-compile-fails covered by battery-2's compilable variants, all killed; M37/M58 re-anchored after the F1/F8 edits, both killed); battery-2 43 killed with exactly the 4 expected survivors (M71/M72 JCS unprovable with ASCII-only closed schemas — reported as bound, not coverage; M92/M95 near-equivalents). Targeted re-verification of all 24 fix mutants: 24/24 killed, each grep-confirmed present, compiling, and reverted.
.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:697:- MUTANT PROTOCOL CAUGHT A MIS-TARGETED TEST: the "expired evidence" case re-signed mutated evidence (new ID) without refreshing the probe's `evidence_ids`, so under the original code it failed at liveness first (right arm, wrong reason to trust), and under a neutered-liveness mutant it failed at the ID-set arm instead of admitting — the test passed for the wrong reason and the mutant survived. Fix: every evidence-mutating case now calls `finalizeProbeIDs` after re-signing (6 cases + platform case), so each refusal lands on its intended arm; the corrected liveness mutant is killed.
.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:705:- F1: `Resolve` returned the struct by value with shared backing arrays, `RegisterExternal` stored the caller record verbatim, `New` shared one protocol array across both built-ins — an in-place mutation converted drift into `terminal_backend_ambiguous` and the registry adopted the change. Pinned by `TestRegistryCopiesSlicesAcrossItsBoundary` (four subtests, incl. the end-to-end duplicate-instead-of-drift bypass).
.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:711:- EVIDENCE: `TASK-260830-2xdt8t_rework-verification.md` (board outcome artifact) with the mutation re-run ratio.
