.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:1021:- ANOMALY: the audit located the part-2 sites as `closed_shapes.go:258, :1506, :1525, :1760`. None of those lines re-checks UTF-8 on any current ref. They match commit `7b94c9ad`, five commits back; the file has moved ~530 lines since. The same commit shows EIGHT `utf8.ValidString` sites, not four — the audit named a subset with no property distinguishing it. Resolved all eight rather than four, because "the clause sweep reports no unexplained survivor" is false while four identical survivors remain.
.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:1024:- FINDING: a first attempt pinned the invariant as "every exported entry point that reaches a re-check also reaches `decodeStrict`". Mutant G survived it: `validateExtensionsObject` reaches `canonicalByteBound` -> `CanonicalByteLength` -> `Canonicalize` -> `decodeStrict`, so transitive reachability of `decodeStrict` is satisfied by a call that never touched the caller's bytes. Reaching a decoder downstream is not the same fact as being decoded by it. Replaced with two properties that are each decidable: no exported entry point reaching a re-check may take a non-`[]byte` parameter, and `json.NewDecoder`/`json.Unmarshal` may appear only inside `decodeStrict`.
.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:1025:- EVIDENCE (part 2): 4 mutants, all killed. D2 adds an exported `map[string]any` entry point reaching the re-checks; G2 adds an exported `[]byte` entry point that decodes with `json.Unmarshal`; E3 deletes one subsumption comment; F3 is the narrowing mutant — the comment stays but names `requireExactMembers` instead of `decodeStrict`.
.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:1038:- FINDING: `validateEnvironmentTuple` enforces `[a-z][a-z0-9.-]{0,63}` on `environment_id` (`closed_shapes.go:733`), but the pinned EnvironmentTuple clause at `SPEC.md:3626-3630` gives that member no type and no format — exactly like the `environment_version`, `store_schema_fingerprint` and `adapter_version` siblings this package already refuses to infer constraints for. The only pinned statement of the grammar is `SPEC.md:3609`, a **Session Adapter Manifest** row. Same cross-schema inference as the 2322 entry, surviving one member over. Production left unchanged and the row now quotes both lines with the open question named; whether `environment-id` is a common type inferable across schemas is a spec question, not a test question.
