.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:1066:- EVIDENCE: 5 mutants, 5 killed, transcript in `TASK-260830-3qrfjp_recovery-mutation-evidence.log`. The three that matter each leave the FAULTED first half of the case passing and die only at a line added in this round. M5 moves the existing artifact but never reports its path (`object_store_fault_test.go:490`). M6 quarantines the mismatched candidate but never reports its path (`:434`). M4 classifies a genuine ABSENCE as an unsafe entry and is killed by all six retry halves at `:247`, `:291`, `:366` (both subtests), and `object_store_fault_unix_test.go:109`, `:147` — the absence-versus-failure-to-read distinction, seen from the recovery side.
