.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:1073:- FINDING: `PutBlob` folded the staged-LENGTH comparison into the same condition as the two source-IDENTITY comparisons: `info.Size() < 0 || uint64(info.Size()) != actualSize || actualSize != expectedSize || actualDigest != expected`. The identity terms compare what the source produced against what the caller declared, which is the SPEC.md Section 3.2 quarantine trigger. The length term compares what the copy ACCEPTED against what the filesystem KEPT, which proves nothing about the source bytes at all. This is the exact write-side mirror of the read-side defect recorded at 2030 today, in the same function, and it survived that fix.
.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:1081:- EVIDENCE: 9 mutants, 9 killed. M1 (delete the length term) installs a TRUNCATED file into the immutable namespace and returns `error = <nil>`. M2 narrows `!=` to `<`: the short case still passes and the over-long case admits — the class-coverage proof a delete-only mutant cannot give. M3 re-merges the branch and the refusal comes back as `ErrIntegrityMismatch` with a quarantined fragment. M7 wraps rebuild inserts as `ErrProjectionCorrupt`; M8 routes a failed rebuild through the quarantine path and reddens with "index-recovery holds 1 directories"; M9 drops the migration rollback and the NEXT open fails `SQLITE_BUSY` on the leaked transaction. Transcript: `TASK-260830-3qrfjp_mutation-evidence.log`.
.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:1094:- EVIDENCE: 8 mutants, 8 killed. M1 (`CanonicalByteLength` returns the marshalled length) reddens all four canonicaljson tests and both config tests. M2-M5 narrow and widen each canonicaljson bound by one; M6-M7 do the same to `maxConfigExtensionBytes`; M8 restores the escaped measurement at the config site alone. Narrow/widen mutants matter here because a delete-only mutant proves the gate exists and says nothing about where it sits. Transcript: `BUG-260902-3v8ck5_mutation-sweep.log`.
.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:1106:- EVIDENCE: 5 mutants, 5 killed; baseline and restored tree both exit 0. Collapsing the classification back (delete the `blobUnreadable` branch, gate quarantine on `verdict == blobUnsafe`) reddens 3 of 4 injected-failure subtests plus the store/projection agreement assertion. Widening `quarantineWarranted` to "any verdict that is not a match" reddens the three pre-existing unsafe-entry tests — the unsafe entry starts getting moved. Narrowing it to `false` and narrowing the mismatch comparison to size-only both redden `TestPutBlobQuarantinesBothInputsWhenExistingDigestPathIsCorrupt`; the size-only mutant is the one that proves the same-size digest disagreement is a real bound, not a delete-only artifact. Making `scanAuthoritativeBlobs` ignore `hooks.openBlob` reddens the agreement test alone, which is what keeps that test from passing on a seam the projection never consults. Evidence: `BUG-260902-1qsdag_mutant-evidence-final.log`.
.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:1115:- DECISION: merged the two bindings into one, keeping `internal/localstore/paths.go:ResolvePaths` as the `production` owner and union-merging `AC-PATH-001` into its `acceptance_cases`. Chosen because nothing else in the registry pins the localstore `ResolvePaths` declaration — `localstore-path-registry` pins `PathDefinitions` and `localstore-layout-owner-only` pins `InitializeLayout` — so the accepted leaf's `-section 3.2` mutant row depends on the binding's `production` field alone, while trunk's §3.2 evidence survives intact through `AC-PATH-001`, whose own `production` is `internal/config/loader.go:Load`. Scoped `tracecheck -section 3.2` now verifies both packages; before the merge each side verified only its own. Every assertion on both sides is preserved and the resolution is strictly stronger than either.
.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:1125:- ROOT CAUSE of why every existing gate stayed green: mutation testing cannot surface an ABSENT clause. There is no operator to rewrite, no literal to shift, no guard to delete. The 47-call-site vocabulary sweep, the derived refusal-coverage gate, the declared-bounds inventory and five seeded fuzz corpora were all satisfied by a validator missing a third of one normative sentence. It was found by reading the spec sentence against the code, which is the only method that finds a clause that is not there.
.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:1129:- DECISION, an over-refusal declined: parent directories are NOT required to be declared. SPEC.md §10.4/§13.14 states no such rule, and the shipped `transferManifestWithEntries(count)` fixture already declares `p/00000` with no `p` entry. Overlap is also compared bytewise, not case-folded — folding does not preserve byte order, so the stack cannot run over folded paths — and that narrowing is disclosed in the artifact row rather than silently assumed.
.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:1130:- EVIDENCE: 7 mutants, 7 killed, 0 survivors, every acceptance case green throughout. Two of them are the pair that proves no tag arm is redundant: restricting the refusal to `file` owners kills only the symlink and hardlink cases, restricting it to non-`file` owners kills only the rest. `BUG-260902-2luo5h_overlap-mutants.log`.
