.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:1213:- EVIDENCE (rework): 18 further single-clause mutants run at this tree from an independent harness (`.temp/BUG-260902-4ajzyz/mutants3.py`, `mutants3b.py`; logs `mutants-rework-01.log`, `-02.log`), each reported with the exact leaf subtests it reddens. The reviewer's live survivor is now KILLED and reddens only the two cases that own the clause — `…BoundIsPinnedAtItsEdge/port_length_upper` and `…DeclaredMeshEndpointGrammar/port_at_length_bound`. Every bound was mutated in both directions where both are expressible; `M11` (label lower bound) kills by making production panic on an empty label, and is reported as such. `M20` (`len(port) < 1` dropped) survives and is equivalent by measurement, not argument: 0 of 9,120 corpus rows differ, while the same corpus separates the `> 5` -> `> 6` narrowing on 178 rows, so it is discriminating rather than blind. Dumps: `equiv-rework-baseline.txt`, `-m19.txt`, `-m20.txt`.
