.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:1259:- CORRECTION (2026-09-02, revision 6): "Both shapes are closed for `core_records.go` in this revision" does not reproduce and is corrected above. The revision-4 grammar rewrote comparison OPERATORS, which cannot express either of the two shapes review then found in `core_records.go`: a boolean-valued `!=` has no operator to rewrite, only a boolean identity to split into `a && !b` / `!a && b`; and `epoch != 1` narrowed to `epoch > 1` is an equivalent mutant, so the operator sweep provably could not reach the `epoch >= 3` narrowing that admitted an epoch-2 lease with a null predecessor. The honest revision-4 claim is: the one-directional EQUALITY-COUPLING shape the operator grammar could express was closed for `core_records.go`; the boolean-identity and literal-boundary shapes were never swept there. Both are closed in revision 6 by standing derived gates, not by a sweep.
.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:1274:- FINDING: `go test ./...` was fully green — seeded fuzz corpora and `tracecheck` included — with **eight normative gates deleted simultaneously** from `internal/canonicaljson/core_records.go`: Safe Boundary `foreground_idle`-true, both `open_*` counters-zero, `accepted_risks` vocabulary and order, workspace member sort/uniqueness, `sanitized_remote_urls` sort/uniqueness, `session.stopped` bootstrap_abort graceful-false, Observation `phase` lower_snake, and Observation stream `+1` continuity. Seven further single-gate narrowings also survived. Package coverage at the time was 87.7%.
