.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:1374:- FINDING: a mechanically derived sweep over the 135 bound arguments and *entry-level* refusal guards in `core_records.go` found 8 survivors the hand-picked sweep never generated — every refusal `ValidateObservationEvent` and `ValidateObservationStream` emit before the event shape is reached (decode failure, non-AX number, non-object, invalid member event, empty stream) plus the `requireArrayMinimum` type guard. All now covered.
.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:1375:- CORRECTION (2026-09-02, revision 4): the sentence above originally read "all 135 bound arguments and refusal guards in `core_records.go`" and "All now covered". That does not reproduce and overstated the sweep. What that sweep enumerated was every *bound argument* plus the guards whose condition it could rewrite to `false`; it was not the refusal-guard set. A statement-coverage profile of the same tree shows **91 runtime refusal branches in `core_records.go` that no test executed once**, at 87.7% package coverage, and the round-3 review deleted eight normative gates simultaneously with `go test ./...` still fully green. The correct claim for revision 3 is: a derived sweep over bound arguments found 8 survivors among the mutants it generated, and said nothing about the refusal-guard set.
.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:1376:- FINDING: the last survivor is an equivalent mutant, not a gap: `requireArrayMinimum`'s absent-member branch is unreachable because its only call site reads `predecessors` after `requireExactMembers` has already refused an omission. Pinned by name rather than deleted.
.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:1388:- ANOMALY: A green mutant is not evidence of subsumption unless the ordering is checked. `Objects()` size bounds survive deletion because `verifyProjectionSchema` runs inside `openProjection` before any `*Projection` is returned; without that ordering the same green result would mean the bound is simply untested.
.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk-mutants-rev14-02/mutation-source/LOGBOOK.md:1393:- ROOT CAUSE: Every fixture for a *shape* clause in `internal/localstore/projection.go` — the checks that refuse a path because it is not the kind of file it must be — was a directory at mode `0700` or a symlink at lstat permission `0777`. Both are refused by the `verifyOwnerFileInfo(info, 0o600)` call on the following line, so the shape clause was reached but never decided anything the suite could observe. Five clauses survived individual disablement; the blob-leaf pair survived being disabled *together*.
